              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rita"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We thought this was the BEST cranberries!! So good with the turkey!! Thanks. Update 2022: We have been making this for 6 years now, and hands down it is the best!",
            "datePublished": "2022-11-24T16:23:58.846Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen Dip"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I do not even like cranberry sauce but my husband insisted he had to have it. This is by far the BEST cranberry sauce I have ever had. Had some leftover and made cranberry oat bars. Recipe is perfect as is.",
            "datePublished": "2018-11-28T08:48:09.667Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Courtney Sholtis"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very nice little recipe. I decided to make it on the stove top right before my turkey was done cooking, hence I had no room for it in the oven. I used around 7 oz of Triple sec and it turned out quite nice and it only took around 20-30 minutes to get it to the desired consistency. \nMy husband really liked it and wants me to make it again for Christmas.",
            "datePublished": "2018-11-22T23:27:30.190Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SoccerMom26"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good. I did not have orange juice so I used the juice of one orange and some zest. I divided the sugar for 1/2 cup brown sugar and 3/4 white sugar. Also didnot have Grand Marnier but used Orange Triple Sec liqueur. Baked in oven for 1 -1/2 hours at 275 in a taller cast iron pan. Other recipes mentioned boiling over but with the lower temp, higher sided pan, I did not have any issues. At the end, I used a potato masher to create thickness. We used the cranberry sauce to mix with BBQ sauce over left over Turkey. It was very awesome!",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-11T23:08:33.927Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carolyn Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made it just as directed and it was perfect. I used Grand Marnier and it added a zip that everyone loved. This recipe will become a Thanksgiving tradition.",
            "datePublished": "2016-11-28T20:03:37.460Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "India520"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So easy and delicious!! After making this just one time, I vow to NEVER EVER buy canned cranberry 'jelly' again!!\nIt tasted so good, that my daughter and I wanted to eat it by itself like it was a pudding. Thank you for the awesome recipe!!",
